<title>UK: LIFFE sugar rangebound and quiet.</title>
<headline>LIFFE sugar rangebound and quiet.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE sugar futures were rangebound and quiet, traders said.</p>
<p>By 1630 GMT May, the most active contract, was up 40 cents at $305.10. May volume was 344 of a total 624 lots.</p>
<p>&quot;They've been stuck in the same range and it doesn't show any sign of breaking, one trader said.</p>
<p>&quot;Most of the trade expect it to go down,&quot; he said. But although New York had tested lows, it had not given an adequate signal to London, he said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
